            <ArticleTitle>Effective headache management. Strategies to help patients gain control over pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>133-6, 139-40, 143-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A general guideline to successful treatment of headache focuses on a diagnosis that satisfies both physician and patient. Thorough history taking, patient and family education, aggressive approaches, and careful follow-up help patients reach therapeutic goals. Successful long-term therapy for headache enables patients to gain control over their symptoms with a combination of carefully selected medications and nonpharmacologic approaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
